# Trace id (Day 5): a correlation id ties one request's logs together across services.
#
# The middleware reuses an incoming x-trace-id header, or mints a new one when the
# caller does not send it, and echoes it back on every response. Look at the
# response headers (not the body) to see it.
#
# Start the server first:  poetry run reviews serve

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### No trace id sent: the server generates one and returns it in the x-trace-id header.
GET {{host}}/health

### A trace id sent by the caller is echoed back unchanged, so the request can be followed.
GET {{host}}/health
x-trace-id: abc123
